      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There are specific reasons why combining sertraline and dextromethorphan can be risky, primarily due to potential serotonin syndrome, which involves signs like confusion, rapid heart rate, and high body temperature. Even though you haven't had issues before, individual metabolic responses vary, and delaying medical advice can allow a minor reaction to escalate into something more dangerous. Given the serious potential side effects, it is generally safer to avoid the medication until you can speak with a professional rather than risk your health just to feel adjusted for sleep.",
      "source": "target",
